Subject: [DSA prefill] fuse the concat + bf16->fp8 cast on the tilelang q path

Base:      sglang git 29481685462732237d80d86076d6563e1f658102
           (python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py is clean at that commit
           in this image; pristine copy in patches/base/)
File:      python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py

Measurement (ISL 8192 / OSL 1024 / concurrency 64 / 192 prompts / TP8, frozen config):

    output_throughput   1478.94 tok/s  vs baseline 1468.358 tok/s   = +0.72%
      arms: results/b_only_r1_20260820_132012 1477.38
            results/b_only_r2_20260820_132251 1480.50
      baseline: 7 runs over 3 server sessions, mean 1468.358, peak-to-peak 0.306%
    Noise floor is 0.39% peak-to-peak across restarts (measured over 21 runs and 9
    server sessions; see FINDINGS.md), so this is ~1.8x the floor -- the smallest
    margin of the three adopted patches. It is carried by 02 being bit-exact and by
    the A-only / B-only / A+B arms being mutually consistent, not by this arm alone.
    This is the smaller of the two changes and the one closest to the floor; the
    two arms bracket the best baseline run (1470.671) without overlapping it.

    Isolated (analysis/bench_dsa_prefill.py, 16384x8, topk 2048, interleaved):
      live cat+cast+tilelang   4.415 ms
      + fused q-prep           4.337 ms   = 1.018x, bit-exact (rel-L2 0.00000)

    Accuracy: gated as part of A+B, gsm8k 5-shot strict-match 0.973465 +/- 0.004427
    vs baseline 0.970432 +/- 0.004666 (eval_results/ab_gate_20260820_125928).

What it does
    tilelang_sparse_fwd casts q to the KV dtype itself, so the stock prefill path
    materialized a bf16 [T, H, 576] via concat_mla_absorb_q_general and then a second
    full fp8 copy of the same shape -- two passes and an extra ~18 MB temporary per
    layer at a 16384-token chunk. concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad does both in one Triton
    kernel; its own docstring calls it a bit-exact replacement for exactly this pair,
    and the decode / flashmla paths in this same file already use it. This tilelang
    prefill branch was the last caller still paying the unfused version.

    Verified bitwise identical to the concat-then-cast it replaces (torch.equal on the
    workload's shape), so this changes cost only, not arithmetic.

    Guarded by _concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad_shape_ok: the helper requires num_heads,
    nope_dim and rope_dim to be powers of two. GLM-5.2 at TP8 gives 8 / 512 / 64;
    anything else falls back to the unfused concat, i.e. to current behaviour.

    No server flag, environment variable or workload parameter is changed.

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py b/python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py
index 37fcbe4042..4a37bfdfe2 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa_backend.py
@@ -86,6 +86,24 @@ from sglang.srt.utils import (
 _DSA_TRITON_PREFILL = get_bool_env_var("SGLANG_DSA_TRITON_PREFILL")
 _IS_GFX95 = is_gfx95_supported()
 
+
+def _concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad_shape_ok(
+    q_nope: torch.Tensor, q_rope: torch.Tensor
+) -> bool:
+    """Whether the fused concat+fp8-cast q-prep kernel accepts these shapes.
+
+    Its docstring requires num_heads / nope_dim / rope_dim to be powers of two (the
+    Triton kernel indexes one program per token with constexpr power-of-two blocks).
+    GLM-5.2 at TP8 gives 8 / 512 / 64, all of which qualify; anything else falls back
+    to the unfused cat, which is what every caller did before.
+    """
+    if q_rope is None or q_nope.dim() != 3 or q_rope.dim() != 3:
+        return False
+    return all(
+        v > 0 and (v & (v - 1)) == 0
+        for v in (q_nope.shape[1], q_nope.shape[2], q_rope.shape[2])
+    )
+
 if is_cuda():
     import deep_gemm
 
@@ -2036,7 +2054,33 @@ class DeepseekSparseAttnBackend(
                         sm_scale=layer.scaling,
                         d_v=layer.v_head_dim,
                     )
-                q_all = concat_mla_absorb_q_general(q_nope, q_rope)
+                # Fuse the concat with the bf16->fp8 cast when the KV cache is fp8.
+                #
+                # tilelang_sparse_fwd casts q to the KV dtype itself, so the stock path
+                # here materializes a bf16 [T, H, 576] via cat and then a second full
+                # [T, H, 576] fp8 copy -- two passes and an extra 18 MB temporary per layer
+                # at a 16384-token chunk. `concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad` does both in one
+                # kernel and is documented as a bit-exact replacement; the decode /
+                # flashmla path already uses it, and this was the last caller still paying
+                # the unfused pair. Measured bit-exact (rel-L2 0.00000) and 1.018x on the
+                # prefill attention op in isolation.
+                _fused_q = None
+                if (
+                    kv_cache.dtype in (torch.float8_e4m3fn, torch.float8_e4m3fnuz)
+                    and _concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad_shape_ok(q_nope, q_rope)
+                ):
+                    _fused_q = q_nope.new_empty(
+                        (q_nope.shape[0], q_nope.shape[1], q_nope.shape[2] + q_rope.shape[2]),
+                        dtype=kv_cache.dtype,
+                    )
+                    concat_and_cast_q_fp8_pad(
+                        _fused_q, q_nope, q_rope, q_nope.shape[1]
+                    )
+                q_all = (
+                    _fused_q
+                    if _fused_q is not None
+                    else concat_mla_absorb_q_general(q_nope, q_rope)
+                )
             return self._forward_tilelang(
                 q_all=q_all,
                 kv_cache=kv_cache,
